From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:46:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: marvell: espressobin: use a finer SD tuning step

On an ESPRESSObin v5 with the root file system on SD, UHS-I SDR104 reads
with ADMA sometimes put wrong data in the page cache: runs of pages
shifted by 8 bytes, starting with the last 8 bytes of an earlier read.
The card and O_DIRECT reads stay correct and nothing is logged.

With the default tuning step divider of 64, 20 of 70 boots under a
compile load showed it, on two cards from different makers. The same
happened with Debian's own 6.12.115 and 7.2.11 kernels. With a divider
of 128 the tuning selects a different sampling point, and 56 of 56
boots were clean, at the same read throughput. 50 MHz high speed,
DDR50, SDR50 and SDR104 with SDMA were clean as well, but slower.

Tested on one ESPRESSObin v5 only; the other variants share this node.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/armada-3720-espressobin.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/armada-3720-espressobin.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/armada-3720-espressobin.dtsi
index fed2dcecb323..93f45dd1b1c3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/armada-3720-espressobin.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/marvell/armada-3720-espressobin.dtsi
@@ -100,6 +100,12 @@ &sdhci1 {
 	cd-gpios = <&gpionb 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	marvell,pad-type = "sd";
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vcc_sd_reg1>;
+	/*
+	 * The default tuning step of 1/64 of the DLL delay picks a sampling
+	 * point at which SDR104 reads with ADMA are silently shifted by 8 bytes
+	 * now and then; 1/128 does not.
+	 */
+	marvell,xenon-phy-tun-step-divider = <128>;
 
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdio_pins>;
